# Publish, Studio finish, affiliate, social

Full rules: `STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §9–§12.

- **Upload:** Data API package (login: `YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN` in `.env` from `npm run youtube:auth`; no database, the ops app is retired): `npm run youtube:package -- --package <…> --video <mp4> --dry-run` first. Private + `publishAt`, explicit `privacyStatus`/`madeForKids`, altered content: yes.
- **One video = one upload:**
  - never swap a file on a live id; never re-upload a public idea;
  - a recut gets a new id, and the old one goes private (not deleted).
- **Long:** normal publish, Sunday 18:00 UK, never a Premiere. Test & Compare with 3 thumbs, end screen, auto-synced captions.
- **Pinned comment:** `07_Content-Ops/scripts/update-pinned-comment.ts --create --video <id> --question "…?"`, then pin it in Studio. Refresh it every Monday with the same script (no `--create`); it only edits the text. `PINNED_COMMENTS.json` holds the ids.
- **Short:** desktop Studio Related → the long it promotes. No new pin, zero `/go/`.
- **Title-only fixes:** `07_Content-Ops/scripts/retitle-videos.ts` (dry run first).
- **Studio-only jobs** go through desktop Studio CDP (`scripts/apply_yellow_white_v04_thumbs.py` pattern; launcher `audits/start_studio_chrome_cdp.sh`). Image-only inputs; never Replace, never `thumbnails.set`.
- **Affiliate:**
  - only on a long that names the product in VO or on screen; one product per film;
  - **paused:** the `/go/` redirect ran on the retired ops app, so no affiliate links until Ben picks a replacement;
  - never invent ASINs; never commit the Amazon tag.
- **Social = Buffer only, automatic** (§12). `youtube:package` schedules the Instagram, Facebook and Threads posts for **exactly** the YouTube go-public time after every live upload; read the `buffer` block in its result. For a Short, the long comes from the package's `relatedVideoId` (`--standalone` if none).
  - Uploaded any other way: `07_Content-Ops/scripts/buffer-mirror.ts mirror --video <id> --long <longId> --media <mp4>` (Short) or `mirror --video <longId> --thumb <jpg>` (long). `plan` = dry run.
  - The Mac runs `buffer-mirror.ts check` daily at 07:05 (LaunchAgent `dev.orbit.buffer-check`). It keeps Buffer in step with Studio and mirrors any scheduled upload not in Buffer yet. Run it yourself straight after a Studio change.
  - **Uploaded by hand (Studio or CDP)?** Run `buffer-mirror.ts register --video <id> --media <mp4> --long <longId>` (or `--thumb <jpg>` for a long) so the check can find the file.
  - Never retype the caption, never use Buffer queue slots, and never set a Buffer time by hand.
  - **TikTok stays paused:** not connected in Buffer, no uploads, retries or "test one".
